1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,374
A grainy black-and-white screen.

2
00:00:02,714 --> 00:00:04,688
A Navy targeting camera, locked onto

3
00:00:04,708 --> 00:00:06,238
something over the Atlantic.

4
00:00:06,808 --> 00:00:08,545
The pilots can't tell what it is.

5
00:00:09,127 --> 00:00:10,827
You can hear it in their voices.

6
00:00:11,397 --> 00:00:13,315
For years, clips like this were rumors.

7
00:00:13,655 --> 00:00:14,214
Leaks.

8
00:00:14,554 --> 00:00:16,701
Copies of copies, passed around online.

9
00:00:17,271 --> 00:00:19,667
Then, in April 2020, the Department of

10
00:00:19,687 --> 00:00:21,573
Defense did something unusual.

11
00:00:22,144 --> 00:00:23,940
It released three of these videos.

12
00:00:24,522 --> 00:00:25,331
Officially.

13
00:00:25,914 --> 00:00:27,949
And it said the objects in them were still

14
00:00:28,907 --> 00:00:30,020
unidentified.

15
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:33,038
So what do those three videos actually

16
00:00:33,058 --> 00:00:33,317
show?

17
00:00:33,787 --> 00:00:35,588
What did the government say about them?

18
00:00:36,058 --> 00:00:37,688
And what has it figured out since?

19
00:00:38,258 --> 00:00:39,531
Let's open the file.

20
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:46,624
Three clips.

21
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:47,864
Two oceans.

22
00:00:48,204 --> 00:00:49,306
A decade apart.

23
00:00:49,926 --> 00:00:52,863
The first is from November 14, 2004.

24
00:00:53,203 --> 00:00:55,340
The USS Nimitz carrier strike group is

25
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:57,212
training off Southern California.

26
00:00:57,552 --> 00:01:00,159
According to CBS News, about 100 miles

27
00:01:00,179 --> 00:01:01,748
southwest of San Diego.

28
00:01:02,318 --> 00:01:04,192
According to his later testimony,

29
00:01:04,212 --> 00:01:06,603
Commander David Fravor led a flight of two

30
00:01:06,623 --> 00:01:08,785
Navy jets sent to check out an unknown

31
00:01:08,805 --> 00:01:09,244
contact.

32
00:01:09,814 --> 00:01:12,170
According to Fravor, he saw a small white

33
00:01:12,190 --> 00:01:13,908
object, shaped like a Tic Tac.

34
00:01:14,328 --> 00:01:15,207
No wings.

35
00:01:15,627 --> 00:01:16,574
No rotors.

36
00:01:17,145 --> 00:01:19,727
He also says the cruiser USS Princeton had

37
00:01:19,747 --> 00:01:22,206
been tracking objects like this on radar

38
00:01:22,226 --> 00:01:24,622
for about two weeks, dropping from very

39
00:01:24,642 --> 00:01:25,490
high altitude.

40
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:28,008
That radar data has not been publicly

41
00:01:28,028 --> 00:01:28,543
released.

42
00:01:29,113 --> 00:01:31,286
Fravor says a second crew went up later

43
00:01:31,306 --> 00:01:33,480
that day, and filmed something with the

44
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,111
jet's infrared targeting pod.

45
00:01:35,451 --> 00:01:36,858
That clip has no sound.

46
00:01:37,198 --> 00:01:39,191
It became known as FLIR1.

47
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:41,933
The camera inside that pod sees heat, not

48
00:01:41,953 --> 00:01:42,254
light.

49
00:01:42,594 --> 00:01:44,208
Warm things glow white, or black,

50
00:01:44,228 --> 00:01:45,446
depending on the setting.

51
00:01:45,786 --> 00:01:47,870
It can lock onto a target miles away.

52
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:50,724
The pilot of the jet that recorded it,

53
00:01:50,744 --> 00:01:52,846
Chad Underwood, later told New York

54
00:01:52,866 --> 00:01:55,332
Magazine he never saw the object with his

55
00:01:55,352 --> 00:01:55,878
own eyes.

56
00:01:56,298 --> 00:01:57,491
Only on the screen.

57
00:01:58,061 --> 00:02:00,612
The other two videos come from January

58
00:02:00,632 --> 00:02:00,950
2015.

59
00:02:01,290 --> 00:02:03,174
A different carrier group, the USS

60
00:02:03,194 --> 00:02:05,470
Theodore Roosevelt, training off the East

61
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:05,806
Coast.

62
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:08,681
Those two clips got the names GIMBAL, and

63
00:02:08,701 --> 00:02:09,078
GOFAST.

64
00:02:09,418 --> 00:02:11,308
The Navy has said both were recorded

65
00:02:11,328 --> 00:02:12,793
during that training period.

66
00:02:13,363 --> 00:02:15,346
Before we go further, let's learn to read

67
00:02:15,366 --> 00:02:15,884
the screen.

68
00:02:16,224 --> 00:02:18,438
Because almost every argument about these

69
00:02:18,458 --> 00:02:20,345
videos comes down to these numbers.

70
00:02:20,915 --> 00:02:22,012
This is GOFAST.

71
00:02:22,352 --> 00:02:24,539
The camera is pointed down at the ocean,

72
00:02:24,559 --> 00:02:26,361
and it's tracking a small object.

73
00:02:26,931 --> 00:02:28,641
Here, the jet's own altitude.

74
00:02:28,981 --> 00:02:30,702
About 25,000 feet.

75
00:02:31,042 --> 00:02:33,031
Here, the camera's angle, pointing down

76
00:02:33,051 --> 00:02:33,958
below the horizon.

77
00:02:34,298 --> 00:02:35,640
And here, RNG.

78
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:38,037
The range to the object, in nautical

79
00:02:38,057 --> 00:02:38,384
miles.

80
00:02:38,954 --> 00:02:40,814
Keep those three numbers in mind.

81
00:02:41,284 --> 00:02:42,279
They'll matter later.

82
00:02:43,099 --> 00:02:45,461
For years, nobody outside the military was

83
00:02:45,481 --> 00:02:47,049
supposed to see any of this.

84
00:02:47,669 --> 00:02:50,465
But according to a Pentagon briefing card

85
00:02:50,485 --> 00:02:52,869
later released under the Freedom of

86
00:02:52,889 --> 00:02:55,685
Information Act, a copy of the 2004 video

87
00:02:55,705 --> 00:02:57,470
was posted online in 2007.

88
00:02:57,810 --> 00:02:58,832
Without permission.

89
00:02:59,403 --> 00:03:00,687
Few people noticed.

90
00:03:01,269 --> 00:03:03,006
That changed ten years later.

91
00:03:03,576 --> 00:03:06,186
On December 16, 2017, The New York Times

92
00:03:06,206 --> 00:03:08,883
published a story about a secret Pentagon

93
00:03:08,903 --> 00:03:11,579
program that had looked into reports like

94
00:03:11,599 --> 00:03:11,974
these.

95
00:03:12,314 --> 00:03:13,747
With it came two videos.

96
00:03:14,087 --> 00:03:15,750
FLIR1, and GIMBAL.

97
00:03:16,319 --> 00:03:18,554
That same month, a private company called

98
00:03:18,574 --> 00:03:20,643
To The Stars Academy put them out too.

99
00:03:20,983 --> 00:03:23,014
A third clip, GOFAST, surfaced a few

100
00:03:23,034 --> 00:03:23,754
months later.

101
00:03:24,325 --> 00:03:26,513
The Pentagon later said those two 2015

102
00:03:26,533 --> 00:03:28,489
clips reached the press through an

103
00:03:28,509 --> 00:03:29,710
unauthorized release.

104
00:03:30,050 --> 00:03:32,299
And the Navy, it said, had no information

105
00:03:32,319 --> 00:03:34,403
on how they were released into general

106
00:03:34,423 --> 00:03:35,067
circulation.

107
00:03:35,637 --> 00:03:38,219
The Times reported that the program had

108
00:03:38,239 --> 00:03:39,353
cost $22 million.

109
00:03:39,693 --> 00:03:41,805
The Pentagon's own description is much

110
00:03:41,825 --> 00:03:42,310
narrower.

111
00:03:42,650 --> 00:03:44,669
It says the effort studied foreign

112
00:03:44,689 --> 00:03:46,888
aerospace threats, and ended in 2012.

113
00:03:47,458 --> 00:03:49,238
So now the videos were everywhere.

114
00:03:49,708 --> 00:03:51,687
But nobody official had confirmed they

115
00:03:51,707 --> 00:03:52,213
were real.

116
00:03:52,932 --> 00:03:55,528
That silence ended in September 2019.

117
00:03:56,148 --> 00:03:58,121
A Navy spokesman, Joseph Gradisher,

118
00:03:58,141 --> 00:03:58,861
confirmed it.

119
00:03:59,201 --> 00:04:01,425
The three videos were copies of official

120
00:04:01,445 --> 00:04:02,154
Navy footage.

121
00:04:02,724 --> 00:04:05,090
He said the Navy considered the objects

122
00:04:05,110 --> 00:04:05,885
unidentified.

123
00:04:06,468 --> 00:04:08,593
And that they had entered Navy training

124
00:04:08,613 --> 00:04:08,978
ranges.

125
00:04:09,548 --> 00:04:11,461
He also pushed back on one claim.

126
00:04:11,801 --> 00:04:13,827
The private company had said the videos

127
00:04:13,847 --> 00:04:15,559
were approved for public release.

128
00:04:15,899 --> 00:04:17,727
According to Gradisher, they were not.

129
00:04:18,297 --> 00:04:20,066
And he used a phrase that would stick.

130
00:04:20,406 --> 00:04:22,308
Unidentified aerial phenomena.

131
00:04:22,648 --> 00:04:23,521
UAP.

132
00:04:23,861 --> 00:04:26,206
Today, the government's preferred term is

133
00:04:26,226 --> 00:04:28,110
unidentified anomalous phenomena.

134
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:29,339
Same letters.

135
00:04:29,679 --> 00:04:31,507
A little more room for things that aren't

136
00:04:31,527 --> 00:04:32,003
in the air.

137
00:04:32,573 --> 00:04:35,121
Then came April 27, 2020.

138
00:04:35,461 --> 00:04:37,702
The Department of Defense put out a short

139
00:04:37,722 --> 00:04:39,963
statement, and posted the three files for

140
00:04:39,983 --> 00:04:41,011
anyone to download.

141
00:04:41,581 --> 00:04:43,094
Notice the word it used.

142
00:04:43,676 --> 00:04:44,752
Unclassified.

143
00:04:45,335 --> 00:04:47,476
These weren't secret documents being

144
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:48,256
declassified.

145
00:04:48,676 --> 00:04:50,702
They were videos that had already leaked,

146
00:04:50,722 --> 00:04:52,050
now released on the record.

147
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:53,968
Why release them at all?

148
00:04:54,438 --> 00:04:56,503
The Pentagon said it wanted to clear up

149
00:04:56,523 --> 00:04:58,428
any misconceptions about whether the

150
00:04:58,448 --> 00:04:59,337
footage was real.

151
00:04:59,907 --> 00:05:02,108
And on what the objects were, it gave one

152
00:05:02,128 --> 00:05:02,487
answer.

153
00:05:03,069 --> 00:05:04,828
They remain unidentified.

154
00:05:05,848 --> 00:05:07,025
There is more footage.

155
00:05:07,365 --> 00:05:09,663
In 2020-two, answering a Freedom of

156
00:05:09,683 --> 00:05:11,849
Information Act request, the Navy

157
00:05:11,869 --> 00:05:14,499
confirmed it holds other UAP videos, but

158
00:05:14,519 --> 00:05:16,089
refused to release them.

159
00:05:16,429 --> 00:05:18,756
It said releasing them would harm national

160
00:05:18,776 --> 00:05:19,259
security.

161
00:05:19,829 --> 00:05:22,791
And in 2025, a Freedom of Information Act

162
00:05:22,811 --> 00:05:25,264
request pried loose 264 pages of a

163
00:05:25,284 --> 00:05:28,173
Pentagon spokesperson's emails about the

164
00:05:28,193 --> 00:05:28,755
release.

165
00:05:29,095 --> 00:05:30,214
Partly redacted.

166
00:05:31,033 --> 00:05:32,903
Videos are one kind of evidence.

167
00:05:33,373 --> 00:05:34,380
People are another.

168
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,121
In July 2023, a House Oversight

169
00:05:37,141 --> 00:05:39,194
subcommittee held a hearing on

170
00:05:39,214 --> 00:05:41,473
unidentified anomalous phenomena.

171
00:05:41,813 --> 00:05:43,331
Every witness was sworn in.

172
00:05:43,901 --> 00:05:46,234
Fravor, now retired, repeated his account

173
00:05:46,254 --> 00:05:46,865
under oath.

174
00:05:47,205 --> 00:05:49,315
He described a white Tic Tac object, and

175
00:05:49,335 --> 00:05:51,391
said his flight got within about half a

176
00:05:51,411 --> 00:05:51,976
mile of it.

177
00:05:52,547 --> 00:05:54,729
In his account, the object turned toward

178
00:05:54,749 --> 00:05:55,665
his jet, climbed,

179
00:05:56,248 --> 00:05:58,299
and then accelerated away, and was gone.

180
00:05:58,869 --> 00:06:01,112
His wingman that day, Alex Dietrich, did

181
00:06:01,132 --> 00:06:01,790
not testify.

182
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:04,543
But in a 2021 television interview, she

183
00:06:04,563 --> 00:06:07,101
said the object moved with no predictable

184
00:06:07,121 --> 00:06:07,787
trajectory.

185
00:06:08,357 --> 00:06:10,447
She also described how it felt to be up

186
00:06:10,467 --> 00:06:12,232
there with something she couldn't

187
00:06:12,252 --> 00:06:12,718
identify.

188
00:06:13,138 --> 00:06:13,968
Exposed.

189
00:06:14,388 --> 00:06:16,259
With nothing to defend themselves.

190
00:06:16,829 --> 00:06:19,089
Then there's Ryan Graves, a former pilot

191
00:06:19,109 --> 00:06:21,369
with Strike Fighter Squadron 11, the Red

192
00:06:21,389 --> 00:06:21,825
Rippers.

193
00:06:22,165 --> 00:06:24,394
In his written testimony, he says GIMBAL

194
00:06:24,414 --> 00:06:26,024
was recorded by his squadron.

195
00:06:26,594 --> 00:06:29,280
In 2019, he told The New York Times that

196
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:31,850
pilots in his squadron saw unexplained

197
00:06:31,870 --> 00:06:34,352
objects almost every day, for months.

198
00:06:34,923 --> 00:06:36,923
In his statement for the hearing, Graves

199
00:06:36,943 --> 00:06:38,591
passed on another pilot's report.

200
00:06:38,931 --> 00:06:41,190
A dark gray cube, inside a clear sphere,

201
00:06:41,210 --> 00:06:42,273
off Virginia Beach.

202
00:06:42,843 --> 00:06:44,859
And the third witness, David Grusch, a

203
00:06:44,879 --> 00:06:47,002
former senior intelligence officer, made

204
00:06:47,022 --> 00:06:47,967
the biggest claim.

205
00:06:48,307 --> 00:06:50,233
He said he had been told of a secret

206
00:06:50,253 --> 00:06:52,017
program to recover crashed craft.

207
00:06:52,587 --> 00:06:54,009
Here's the key detail.

208
00:06:54,592 --> 00:06:56,861
He said his testimony was based on what

209
00:06:56,881 --> 00:06:57,801
others told him.

210
00:06:58,221 --> 00:07:00,412
And the Pentagon says it has found no

211
00:07:00,432 --> 00:07:02,624
verifiable evidence for programs like

212
00:07:02,644 --> 00:07:02,923
that.

213
00:07:03,743 --> 00:07:05,395
So, what does the government's own

214
00:07:05,415 --> 00:07:06,035
analysis say?

215
00:07:06,654 --> 00:07:09,099
In June 2021, the Office of the Director

216
00:07:09,119 --> 00:07:11,441
of National Intelligence published its

217
00:07:11,461 --> 00:07:12,919
first public assessment.

218
00:07:13,259 --> 00:07:15,783
It looked at 144 reports from U.S.

219
00:07:15,803 --> 00:07:17,204
government sources.

220
00:07:17,774 --> 00:07:18,732
It could explain

221
00:07:19,315 --> 00:07:19,836
one.

222
00:07:20,418 --> 00:07:22,123
A large, deflating balloon.

223
00:07:23,044 --> 00:07:24,744
The report had other numbers worth

224
00:07:24,764 --> 00:07:25,149
knowing.

225
00:07:25,489 --> 00:07:27,886
80 of the reports involved more than one

226
00:07:27,906 --> 00:07:28,309
sensor.

227
00:07:28,649 --> 00:07:31,082
In eighteen incidents, observers reported

228
00:07:31,102 --> 00:07:32,638
unusual movement or flight

229
00:07:32,658 --> 00:07:33,596
characteristics.

230
00:07:33,936 --> 00:07:36,169
And pilots reported eleven near-misses.

231
00:07:36,739 --> 00:07:39,125
It also listed five possible kinds of

232
00:07:39,145 --> 00:07:39,905
explanation.

233
00:07:40,325 --> 00:07:42,574
Airborne clutter, like balloons and birds.

234
00:07:42,994 --> 00:07:44,731
Natural atmospheric effects.

235
00:07:45,151 --> 00:07:47,950
U.S. government or industry developmental

236
00:07:47,970 --> 00:07:48,568
programs.

237
00:07:48,988 --> 00:07:50,619
Foreign adversary systems.

238
00:07:51,201 --> 00:07:53,130
And a category called, simply, other.

239
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:56,053
A year later, in July 2020-two, the

240
00:07:56,073 --> 00:07:58,629
Pentagon created a dedicated office to

241
00:07:58,649 --> 00:07:59,442
investigate.

242
00:07:59,782 --> 00:08:02,197
The All-domain Anomaly Resolution Office.

243
00:08:02,537 --> 00:08:03,191
AARO.

244
00:08:03,531 --> 00:08:06,723
Its first big count, published in early

245
00:08:06,743 --> 00:08:09,934
2023, brought the total to 510 reports,

246
00:08:09,954 --> 00:08:11,828
including 366 new ones.

247
00:08:12,398 --> 00:08:15,868
Of those 366, 163 were balloons or

248
00:08:15,888 --> 00:08:17,202
balloon-like.

249
00:08:17,542 --> 00:08:19,540
26 were drones, or drone-like.

250
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:20,870
Six were clutter.

251
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:24,272
And 171 were still uncharacterized.

252
00:08:24,842 --> 00:08:26,972
Since then, analysts have worked through

253
00:08:26,992 --> 00:08:28,046
hundreds more cases.

254
00:08:28,386 --> 00:08:30,606
And one of the famous Navy videos now has

255
00:08:30,626 --> 00:08:31,643
an official answer.

256
00:08:32,213 --> 00:08:34,416
Remember those three numbers on the GOFAST

257
00:08:34,436 --> 00:08:34,787
screen?

258
00:08:35,257 --> 00:08:36,509
Here's where they come in.

259
00:08:37,079 --> 00:08:39,437
If you know how high the jet is, which way

260
00:08:39,457 --> 00:08:41,646
the camera points, and how far away the

261
00:08:41,666 --> 00:08:43,741
object is, you can work out where the

262
00:08:43,761 --> 00:08:44,704
object really is.

263
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:48,504
In 2023, a NASA study team did that math.

264
00:08:48,924 --> 00:08:51,717
It put the object at about 13,000 feet.

265
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:53,669
Not skimming the water.

266
00:08:54,251 --> 00:08:56,159
Halfway between the jet and the sea.

267
00:08:56,729 --> 00:08:57,586
And its speed?

268
00:08:58,106 --> 00:08:59,598
About 40 mph.

269
00:08:59,938 --> 00:09:01,915
Roughly what the wind does at that height.

270
00:09:02,485 --> 00:09:04,089
So why does it look so fast?

271
00:09:04,609 --> 00:09:06,562
Because the camera is on a jet doing

272
00:09:06,582 --> 00:09:07,988
hundreds of miles an hour.

273
00:09:08,328 --> 00:09:09,873
The background rushes past.

274
00:09:10,343 --> 00:09:11,840
The object barely moves.

275
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:13,325
It's called parallax.

276
00:09:13,895 --> 00:09:16,265
In November 2024, AARO's director, Jon

277
00:09:16,285 --> 00:09:18,655
Kosloski, told a Senate Armed Services

278
00:09:18,675 --> 00:09:21,296
subcommittee the office had assessed, with

279
00:09:21,316 --> 00:09:23,812
high confidence, that the object was not

280
00:09:23,832 --> 00:09:25,573
actually close to the water.

281
00:09:26,143 --> 00:09:28,801
Less than three months later, in February

282
00:09:28,821 --> 00:09:31,545
2025, AARO published its formal resolution

283
00:09:31,565 --> 00:09:32,328
of the case.

284
00:09:32,668 --> 00:09:33,754
Same altitude.

285
00:09:34,094 --> 00:09:35,298
Same explanation.

286
00:09:35,638 --> 00:09:37,911
It said the object was consistent with a

287
00:09:37,931 --> 00:09:40,260
small airborne object, such as a balloon,

288
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:40,890
or a drone.

289
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:43,581
AARO was also clear about the limits.

290
00:09:43,921 --> 00:09:46,218
The original file and its data were lost.

291
00:09:46,558 --> 00:09:48,962
It worked from the public 34-second clip.

292
00:09:49,302 --> 00:09:51,609
And it never identified exactly what the

293
00:09:51,629 --> 00:09:52,249
object was.

294
00:09:52,819 --> 00:09:54,551
Critics have pointed out other gaps.

295
00:09:54,891 --> 00:09:57,273
Writing in the Daily Grail, one noted that

296
00:09:57,293 --> 00:09:59,388
AARO didn't interview the pilots, and

297
00:09:59,408 --> 00:10:01,332
didn't estimate the object's size.

298
00:10:01,902 --> 00:10:03,218
What about the other two?

299
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:05,372
Here, the record gets thin.

300
00:10:05,942 --> 00:10:08,050
For GIMBAL, some independent analysts

301
00:10:08,070 --> 00:10:10,351
argue the shape is infrared glare from a

302
00:10:10,371 --> 00:10:12,710
distant jet engine, and that the rotation

303
00:10:12,730 --> 00:10:14,378
comes from the camera itself.

304
00:10:14,718 --> 00:10:15,916
Others dispute that.

305
00:10:16,386 --> 00:10:17,280
It's a theory.

306
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:19,803
No government body has endorsed it, or

307
00:10:19,823 --> 00:10:20,557
ruled it out.

308
00:10:21,127 --> 00:10:23,751
And FLIR1, the Tic Tac video, has no

309
00:10:23,771 --> 00:10:25,808
official explanation either.

310
00:10:26,390 --> 00:10:27,567
Not from the Navy.

311
00:10:27,988 --> 00:10:29,154
Not from AARO.

312
00:10:30,074 --> 00:10:31,379
Which brings us to now.

313
00:10:31,999 --> 00:10:34,736
In 2026, the release of government UAP

314
00:10:34,756 --> 00:10:36,477
records picked up speed.

315
00:10:36,817 --> 00:10:39,209
According to The Washington Post, the

316
00:10:39,229 --> 00:10:41,947
president directed agencies in February to

317
00:10:41,967 --> 00:10:44,554
identify and declassify their UAP files.

318
00:10:45,124 --> 00:10:47,225
In May, the Pentagon launched a public

319
00:10:47,245 --> 00:10:49,402
website for releasing those records, in

320
00:10:49,422 --> 00:10:49,848
batches.

321
00:10:50,188 --> 00:10:53,695
And in July, AARO's latest annual report

322
00:10:53,715 --> 00:10:57,221
counted 319 new cases, and 370 resolved.

323
00:10:57,791 --> 00:11:00,183
Every one of those resolved cases had an

324
00:11:00,203 --> 00:11:02,595
ordinary explanation, according to AARO.

325
00:11:03,165 --> 00:11:04,758
And Congress is still pushing.

326
00:11:05,098 --> 00:11:07,741
In July, the House adopted an amendment to

327
00:11:07,761 --> 00:11:10,341
create a formal UAP records collection at

328
00:11:10,361 --> 00:11:11,736
the National Archives.

329
00:11:12,206 --> 00:11:13,943
As of this video, it isn't law.

330
00:11:14,513 --> 00:11:16,154
So here's where the file stands.

331
00:11:16,674 --> 00:11:19,041
Three videos, recorded by Navy crews,

332
00:11:19,061 --> 00:11:20,848
officially released in 2020.

333
00:11:21,318 --> 00:11:23,180
One of them, GOFAST, has an official

334
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:23,546
answer.

335
00:11:23,886 --> 00:11:25,832
Most likely, something small, drifting on

336
00:11:25,852 --> 00:11:26,263
the wind.

337
00:11:26,833 --> 00:11:28,805
The other two are still officially

338
00:11:28,825 --> 00:11:29,567
unidentified.

339
00:11:30,150 --> 00:11:31,791
That doesn't mean they're alien.

340
00:11:32,211 --> 00:11:34,232
It means the government hasn't published

341
00:11:34,252 --> 00:11:34,742
an answer.

342
00:11:35,312 --> 00:11:37,561
And that's the real story of these videos.

343
00:11:38,144 --> 00:11:39,550
Not proof of anything.

344
00:11:40,132 --> 00:11:40,872
A record.

345
00:11:41,292 --> 00:11:42,869
One that's still being written.

346
00:11:43,689 --> 00:11:45,649
If there's a government file you want us

347
00:11:45,669 --> 00:11:47,282
to open, tell us in the comments.

348
00:11:47,622 --> 00:11:48,730
We read every one.

349
